{
  "id": "becker-doring-five-clusters-second-biology",
  "name": "Closed five-size Becker-Doering cluster assembly",
  "description": "Monomer attachment/detachment with explicit dimer stoichiometry and conserved monomer mass. A finite closed chain, not a quantitative supersaturated-vapor nucleation-rate prediction. Illustrative attachment1,detachment0.1,monomer1,largerclusters0. No flux beyond size5; there is no artificial sink at the truncation. Horizon100 and RK4step0.02 chosen for equilibration. https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc62899/ Signed net-rate flows encode the stated differential equations. No clamps or resets. These educational equations are not fitted biological forecasts.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1002/andp.19354160806",
  "reference": "Becker and Doering (1935), Kinetische Behandlung der Keimbildung in uebersaettigten Daempfen; NACA TM1374 (1954) English translation. Finite closed truncation is our adaptation.",
